      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix the lemongrass, garlic, fish sauce, sugar, and sesame oil. Toss with the sliced pork. Marinate for at least 1 hour."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pickle the carrot and daikon: toss with 1 tbsp lime juice, 1 tsp sugar, and a pinch of seasoning. Leave for 30 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make the nước chấm dressing: mix the fish sauce, lime juice, sugar, garlic, chilli, and 4 tbsp of water. Stir until the sugar dissolves."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cook the rice vermicelli according to the packet. Drain, rinse with cold water, and leave at room temperature."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the griddle pan to high. Add the oil and grill the pork in a single layer for 2 to 3 minutes per side until caramelised and cooked through."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Divide the noodles between 4 bowls. Top with grilled pork, bean sprouts, fresh herbs, and drained pickled vegetables. Scatter with peanuts."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour the nước chấm dressing over the bowl just before eating. Toss everything together."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The noodles clump together into a solid block.",
              "cause": "They were not rinsed with cold water or tossed after draining.",
              "fix": "Rinse the cooked noodles immediately under cold water and toss with a drizzle of oil. Separate the strands by hand if needed."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The pork is tough and dry.",
              "cause": "The slices were too thick or the grill was not hot enough.",
              "fix": "Slice pork as thin as possible. Get the pan very hot before adding the pork. Thin slices need only 2 minutes per side."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The bowl tastes flat even with the dressing added.",
              "cause": "The dressing was too diluted or the pork was under-seasoned.",
              "fix": "Add more fish sauce to the dressing. The pork marinade should also taste quite salty and sweet before grilling - it mellows on the grill."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bún thịt nướng is popular across Vietnam, especially in the south and centre of the country. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is a common lunch dish sold at street stalls and small restaurants. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The bowl format . noodles, grilled protein, herbs, and dressing . is one of the foundations of Vietnamese cooking. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The dish is eaten at room temperature, which makes it different from most noodle soups. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Outside Vietnam, it is one of the most popular dishes at Vietnamese restaurants worldwide."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
